y decade (76). Springfield's all-time high is 112\u00b0F, on July 14, 1954.","t_chg":"Springfield's days got warmer. Its nights didn't.","p_chg":"Across 146 complete years: Springfield's average low shows no clear change: \u22120.05\u00b0F per decade, a range (\u22120.11 to +0.02) that includes zero. Springfield's average high has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.15\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.09 to +0.22), about +2.2\u00b0F since 1880.","t_mon":"Lows rose in none; September and October fell. Highs rose in 7 of 12 months.","t_rain":"Rain and snow: no clear long-term change","p_rain":"Springfield's yearly precipitation shows no clear long-term change (+0.12 inches per decade, a range that includes zero). The 1991\u20132020 normal is 38.0 inches a year. The wettest year was 1882 (58.21 in); the driest, 1914 (22.76 in).","show_snow":true,"sig_bars":{"lo":false,"hi":false},"t_year":"2026 so far: 11 daily record highs, 1 daily record low"}}